nodecode-clef is a rewrite of MelMayssonOwen's MelMayssonOwen/hermes-plugins:

  https://github.com/MelMayssonOwen/hermes-plugins
  commit f203c3f897784d731ef48bc0974104a4d08cf5f8
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Opsibyte (LICENSE)

The original is an Agent Plugins v1 package: plugin.json, an mcp.json naming
the streamable-HTTP server https://clefdrills.com/mcp, and one skill under
skills/ that taught the model when to call the four tools the server lists.
The rewrite keeps all four tools (find_music_guides, transpose_chords,
spell_piano_chord, tab_to_piano_notes) with the server's own member names,
talked to directly as JSON-RPC over the image's own HTTP call instead of by
an MCP client, and answers them as lines rather than JSON envelopes; the
plugin's offline transposition helper (skills/clef-music-tools/scripts/
transpose.py) is ported into chords.lisp, so transpose_chords needs no server.
Left out: the MCP package manifest and the skill's prose. Nodecode cells are
directories and a slash command, not Agent Plugins packages, and the drills
and practice instructions the skill carried are teaching text the model is
given here as a manual topic's primer rather than as a skill file. The tool
list is also no longer discovered from the server at run time, which is the
one place it could change under the cell.
